body:
I get this issue when using imports from another package in our monorepo via symlinks with RC.4

Edit: I also tried to import MaxCharactersPipe without the module. Not sure if it was the exact same error. But it was an error none the less. I was never able to compile my project at all.

``` 
ERROR in Unable to write a reference to MaxCharactersPipe in 
    C:/Users/user/repo/mono/packages/some-package/node_modules/@mono/another-package/src/pipes/max-characters.pipe.ts 
from 
    C:/Users/user/repo/mono/packages/some-package/node_modules/@mono/another-package/src/pipes/pipes.module.ts
```

```
#wepack.config.ts
new AngularCompilerPlugin({
    tsConfigPath: helpers.rootPath('tsconfig.json'),
    mainPath: helpers.rootPath('src/main.ts'),
    sourceMap: true,
    compilerOptions: {
        enableIvy: true
    } as any
})
```

```
#pipes.module.ts
import { NgModule } from '@angular/core';
import { MaxCharactersPipe } from './max-characters.pipe';

@NgModule({
    declarations: [
        MaxCharactersPipe
    ],
    exports: [
        MaxCharactersPipe
    ]
})
export class PipesModule { }
```
```
#app.module.ts
import  { PipesModule } from '@mono/another-package'

@NgModule({
    imports: [
        ...
        PipesModule
    ]
})
```
```
#package.json
{
  "dependencies": {
    "@mono/another-package": "file:../another-package"
  }
}
```
